In HubSpot email templates, you can access custom properties sent via the single-send API using HubL (HubSpot's templating language). Here's how to build your template:

```html
{# Access the custom properties #}
{% set order_total = contact.customProperties.order_total %}
{% set is_member = contact.customProperties.is_member %}

{# Display order total #}
<p>Order Total: {{ order_total }}</p>

{# Conditional members-only block #}
{% if is_member %}
  <div class="members-only">
    <h2>Exclusive Member Benefits</h2>
    <p>Thank you for being a valued member! Here are your exclusive perks...</p>
  </div>
{% endif %}
```

**Key points:**

1. **Custom properties** are accessed via `contact.customProperties.property_name`
2. **Conditional logic** uses `{% if condition %}...{% endif %}`
3. The `is_member` boolean will work directly in the `if` statement
4. You can format the `order_total` if needed: `{{ order_total|format_currency }}`

**Alternative approach** for better readability:

```html
{% set props = contact.customProperties %}

<p>Order Total: {{ props.order_total|format_currency }}</p>

{% if props.is_member == true %}
  <!-- Members-only content -->
{% endif %}
```

Make sure to test with sample data in HubSpot's email editor using the "Preview with contact" feature to verify the conditional rendering works as expected.

