with_skill.response:
Looking at your module, I can see four bugs that explain exactly what you're seeing:

## 1. The blank firstname issue

```hubl
{{ contact.firstname|default("there") }}
```

**Filters don't apply to personalization tokens in email.** HubSpot documents this explicitly: *"You can apply HubL filters to personalization tokens on HubSpot CMS and blog pages, but not in emails."* The `|default()` is doing nothing, so contacts with no firstname render blank.

**Fix:**
```hubl
{{ personalization_token("contact.firstname", "there") }}
```

Or set a global fallback at Settings → Marketing → Email → Personalization.

## 2. The `elsif` typo

```hubl
{% elsif contact.lifecyclestage == "lead" %}
```

**It's `{% elif %}` in HubL**, not `elsif` (that's Liquid). This is a hard error that breaks the entire conditional.

**Fix:**
```hubl
{% elif contact.lifecyclestage == "lead" %}
```

## 3. The deal list never renders

```hubl
{% for deal in crm_objects("deal", "dealstage=closedwon&limit=5", "dealname,amount") %}
```

**`crm_objects()` returns a wrapper object**, not a list. The shape is `{has_more, offset, total, results}`. You're iterating the wrapper, which renders nothing.

**Fix:**
```hubl
{% for deal in crm_objects("deal", "dealstage=closedwon&limit=5", "dealname,amount").results %}
```

## 4. Lifetime value always prints 0

```hubl
{% set total = 0 %}
{% for deal in ... %}
  {% set total = total + deal.amount %}
{% endfor %}
<p>Lifetime value: {{ total }}</p>
```

**Loop scope.** HubSpot documents: *"Any variables defined within loops are limited to the scope of that loop and cannot be called from outside of the loop."* The `total` set inside dies at `{% endfor %}`, so you print the original 0.

**Fix — use a filter instead:**
```hubl
{% set deals = crm_objects("deal", "dealstage=closedwon&limit=5", "dealname,amount") %}
{% for deal in deals.results %}
  <p>{{ deal.dealname }} - {{ deal.amount }}</p>
{% endfor %}
<p>Lifetime value: {{ deals.results|sum(attribute="amount") }}</p>
```

---

## Fixed module

```hubl
{% if contact.lifecyclestage == "customer" %}
  <p>Hi {{ personalization_token("contact.firstname", "there") }},</p>
{% elif contact.lifecyclestage == "lead" %}
  <p>Hi there,</p>
{% endif %}

{% set deals = crm_objects("deal", "dealstage=closedwon&limit=5", "dealname,amount") %}
{% if deals.results %}
  {% for deal in deals.results %}
    <p>{{ deal.dealname }} - {{ deal.amount }}</p>
  {% endfor %}
  <p>Lifetime value: {{ deals.results|sum(attribute="amount") }}</p>
{% else %}
  <p>Browse our offerings to get started.</p>
{% endif %}
```

I added an `{% else %}` branch for the zero-deals case — HubSpot's own guidance is to include fallback data so a query that matches nothing doesn't produce a blank email.

**Why it previewed fine for you:** You're likely a customer with firstname set and won deals, so your specific data made every branch work. The bugs only surface across the broader list.

**One more thing:** This uses `crm_objects()`, which counts against HubSpot's function limits — one of a documented maximum of **5 CRM functions per email**, with a **500,000 recipient ceiling** for a single-function email. Make sure the module has **Use module for programmable email** toggled on, or it won't render.

